<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
<title>ESP Flasher</title>
<style>
  :root{
    --bg:#0f171e; --panel:#16212b; --ink:#dde6ed; --soft:#a2b2bf; --faint:#75889a;
    --rule:#283742; --teal:#48bacc; --good:#5fbf85; --warn:#d6a43c; --bad:#e4736d;
  }
  *,*::before,*::after{box-sizing:border-box}
  body{margin:0;background:var(--bg);color:var(--ink);
    font:15px/1.6 system-ui,-apple-system,"Segoe UI",sans-serif;padding:26px 20px 70px}
  .wrap{max-width:820px;margin:0 auto}
  h1{font-size:1.5rem;margin:0 0 4px;letter-spacing:-.01em}
  .sub{color:var(--soft);margin:0 0 24px;font-size:.95rem}
  .card{background:var(--panel);border:1px solid var(--rule);border-radius:8px;
    padding:17px 19px;margin:0 0 16px}
  .card h2{font-size:1.02rem;margin:0 0 4px}
  .card .hint{color:var(--faint);font-size:.86rem;margin:0 0 12px}
  code{font-family:ui-monospace,"SF Mono",Menlo,monospace;font-size:.86em;
    background:#1b2732;color:#cfe;padding:.12em .38em;border-radius:3px}
  a{color:var(--teal)} .muted{color:var(--faint);font-size:.88rem}
  ol{margin:0;padding-left:1.15em} li{margin-bottom:.45em}

  #gate{border-left:3px solid var(--warn)}
  #gate.ok{border-left-color:var(--good)}
  #gate.bad{border-left-color:var(--bad)}
  .badge{display:inline-block;font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;
    padding:.18em .5em;border-radius:3px;margin-left:.4em;vertical-align:2px}
  .badge.ok{background:#12341f;color:var(--good)}
  .badge.bad{background:#3a1b1a;color:var(--bad)}

  .chips{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(215px,1fr));gap:8px}
  .chip{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px;text-align:left;cursor:pointer;
    background:#111a22;border:1px solid var(--rule);border-radius:6px;padding:9px 11px;
    color:var(--ink);font:inherit;font-size:.88rem;transition:border-color .12s}
  .chip:hover{border-color:var(--teal)}
  .chip.on{border-color:var(--teal);background:#12262c}
  .chip-name{font-weight:600;line-height:1.3}
  .chip-chip{color:var(--faint);font-size:.74rem;letter-spacing:.04em}
  .chip:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--teal);outline-offset:2px}

  .lessons{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:6px}
  .lesson{background:#111a22;border:1px solid var(--rule);border-radius:5px;
    padding:5px 9px;font-size:.82rem;text-decoration:none;color:var(--soft)}
  .lesson:hover{border-color:var(--teal);color:var(--ink)}

  esp-web-install-button{display:block;margin-top:12px}
  #chosen{margin:10px 0 0;font-size:.9rem;color:var(--soft)}
</style>
</head>
<body data-gallery="{{GALLERY_URL}}">
<div class="wrap">

  <h1>ESP Flasher</h1>
  <p class="sub">Flash a board and set its Wi-Fi over USB — from this sidebar.</p>

  <!-- Rendered pessimistic on purpose: if app.js is blocked, the page must not
       look like it is ready. -->
  <div class="card" id="gate">
    <h2>Browser check <span class="badge bad" id="gate-badge">checking…</span></h2>
    <div id="gate-body" class="muted">
      If this never changes, JavaScript was blocked and the flasher cannot run.
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <h2>Before you connect</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Stop anything reading the board's serial port — a logger or bridge
        <strong>holds it</strong> and the browser will not see the device.<br>
        <span class="muted">e.g. <code>pkill -f serial-to-mqtt</code></span></li>
      <li>Plug the board into <strong>this computer</strong> — the one running the
        browser, not the Home Assistant host.</li>
      <li>Pick a firmware, press <em>Connect</em>. Already-flashed board? Choose
        <em>Configure Wi-Fi</em> instead of installing.</li>
    </ol>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <h2>Workshop firmwares</h2>
    <p class="hint" id="chars-note">loading…</p>
    <div class="chips" id="chars"></div>
    <p id="chosen" class="muted">Nothing selected yet.</p>
    <esp-web-install-button id="btn">
      <button slot="activate">Connect to a board</button>
      <span slot="unsupported">This browser cannot do Web Serial — see the check above.</span>
      <span slot="not-allowed">Not a secure context — see the check above.</span>
    </esp-web-install-button>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <h2>kru32 — ESP32 display lessons</h2>
    <p class="hint">LVGL and display work, lesson by lesson. These are the configs the
      <code>ancs-display</code> firmware copies its known-good pin values from.</p>
    <div class="lessons" id="lessons"></div>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <h2>Sources</h2>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:0">
      <a href="{{GALLERY_URL}}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">workshop-04-esp32-wasm gallery</a><br>
      <a href="https://github.com/the-oracle-keeps-the-human-human/kru32-oracle" target="_blank" rel="noopener">kru32-oracle</a><br>
      <a href="https://github.com/dustboy-kit/esp32c3-pm25-monitor" target="_blank" rel="noopener">dustboy-kit/esp32c3-pm25-monitor</a> — DBK PM2.5 firmware
    </p>
  </div>

</div>
<script src="app.js"></script>
<script type="module" src="https://unpkg.com/esp-web-tools@9.4.3/dist/web/install-button.js?module"></script>
</body>
</html>
